{"id":"mahabharata-3-199","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":199,"title":"नवनवत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 199 · The hunter on his trade and on harm","summary":{"en":"The dharmavyadha explains that he sells meat but does not kill, following the trade of his birth honestly, and is devoted to truth, gifts and service. He argues that no one lives without harming some creature, and that doing one's own duty well brings honour.","kn":"ತಾನು ಮಾಂಸ ಮಾರುತ್ತೇನೆ ಆದರೆ ಕೊಲ್ಲುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಹುಟ್ಟಿನ ವೃತ್ತಿಯನ್ನು ಪ್ರಾಮಾಣಿಕವಾಗಿ ನಡೆಸುತ್ತೇನೆ, ಸತ್ಯ, ದಾನ, ಸೇವೆಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ನಿರತನಾಗಿದ್ದೇನೆ ಎಂದು ಧರ್ಮವ್ಯಾಧನು ವಿವರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಯಾವ ಜೀವಿಗೂ ಹಾನಿ ಮಾಡದೆ ಯಾರೂ ಬದುಕಲಾರರು, ಸ್ವಧರ್ಮವನ್ನು ಚೆನ್ನಾಗಿ ಮಾಡುವುದೇ ಕೀರ್ತಿ ತರುತ್ತದೆ ಎಂದು ವಾದಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धर्मव्याध बताता है कि वह मांस बेचता है पर मारता नहीं, अपने जन्म के व्यवसाय को ईमानदारी से करता है और सत्य, दान और सेवा में लगा रहता है। वह तर्क देता है कि कोई भी किसी प्राणी को हानि पहुँचाए बिना नहीं जीता, और अपना कर्तव्य भली-भाँति करना ही यश देता है।","te":"తాను మాంసం అమ్ముతాను కానీ చంపను, జన్మతో వచ్చిన వృత్తిని నిజాయితీగా నడుపుతాను, సత్యం, దానం, సేవలో నిరతుడనని ధర్మవ్యాధుడు వివరిస్తాడు. ఏ జీవికీ హాని చేయకుండా ఎవరూ బ్రతకలేరని, స్వధర్మాన్ని బాగా ఆచరించడమే కీర్తిని ఇస్తుందని వాదిస్తాడు.","ta":"தான் இறைச்சி விற்பேன் ஆனால் கொல்வதில்லை, பிறப்பால் வந்த தொழிலை நேர்மையாகச் செய்கிறேன், உண்மை, கொடை, பணிவிடையில் ஈடுபட்டுள்ளேன் என்று தர்மவ்யாதன் விளக்குகிறான். எந்த உயிருக்கும் தீங்கிழைக்காமல் யாரும் வாழ முடியாது, தன் கடமையை நன்கு செய்வதே புகழ் தரும் என்று வாதிடுகிறான்.","ml":"താൻ മാംസം വിൽക്കുന്നുവെങ്കിലും കൊല്ലുന്നില്ലെന്ന് ധർമ്മവ്യാധൻ വിശദീകരിക്കുന്നു; ജന്മം കൊണ്ട് കിട്ടിയ തൊഴിൽ സത്യസന്ധമായി ചെയ്യുന്നവനാണ് താൻ; സത്യം, ദാനം, സേവനം എന്നിവയോട് അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് ഭക്തിയുണ്ട്. ഏതെങ്കിലും ജീവിയെ ഉപദ്രവിക്കാതെ ആരും ജീവിക്കില്ലെന്നും, സ്വന്തം കർത്തവ്യം നന്നായി ചെയ്യുന്നത് ബഹുമാനം നൽകുമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം വാദിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.199; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"स तु विप्रमथोवाच धर्मव्याधो युधिष्ठिर ।\nयदहं ह्याचरे कर्म घोरमेतदसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The dharma-hunter then said to the brahmin, Yudhishthira: \"The work I do is undoubtedly cruel."}},{"n":2,"text":"विधिस्तु बलवान्ब्रह्मन्दुस्तरं हि पुराकृतम् ।\nपुराकृतस्य पापस्य कर्मदोषो भवत्ययम् ।\nदोषस्यैतस्य वै ब्रह्मन्विघाते यत्नवानहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But destiny is powerful, brahmin, and what was done before is hard to cross. This fault of action comes from sin done in the past, and I am striving to remove this fault."}},{"n":3,"text":"विधिना विहिते पूर्वं निमित्तं घातको भवेत् ।\nनिमित्तभूता हि वयं कर्मणोऽस्य द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is ordained in advance by destiny, the killer is only the occasion; we are only the instruments of this deed, best of brahmins."}},{"n":4,"text":"येषां हतानां मांसानि विक्रीणामो वयं द्विज ।\nतेषामपि भवेद्धर्म उपभोगेन भक्षणात् ।\nदेवतातिथिभृत्यानां पितॄणां प्रतिपूजनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those whose slain flesh we sell, brahmin, also gain merit through the eating and enjoyment of it, and through worship of the gods, guests, dependants and ancestors."}},{"n":5,"text":"ओषध्यो वीरुधश्चापि पशवो मृगपक्षिणः ।\nअन्नाद्यभूता लोकस्य इत्यपि श्रूयते श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Plants, creepers, cattle, deer and birds are made as food for the world; so too scripture is heard."}},{"n":6,"text":"आत्ममांसप्रदानेन शिबिरौशीनरो नृपः ।\nस्वर्गं सुदुर्लभं प्राप्तः क्षमावान्द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"By giving his own flesh, King Shibi Aushinara, the patient one, reached a heaven very hard to reach, best of brahmins."}},{"n":7,"text":"राज्ञो महानसे पूर्वं रन्तिदेवस्य वै द्विज ।\nद्वे सहस्रे तु वध्येते पशूनामन्वहं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In King Rantideva's kitchen in the old days, two thousand animals were killed every day, brahmin."}},{"n":8,"text":"समांसं ददतो ह्यन्नं रन्तिदेवस्य नित्यशः ।\nअतुला कीर्तिरभवन्नृपस्य द्विजसत्तम ।\nचातुर्मास्येषु पशवो वध्यन्त इति नित्यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For giving food with meat constantly, Rantideva's fame was unequalled, best of brahmins, because animals were killed constantly during the four-month rites."}},{"n":9,"text":"अग्नयो मांसकामाश्च इत्यपि श्रूयते श्रुतिः ।\nयज्ञेषु पशवो ब्रह्मन्वध्यन्ते सततं द्विजैः ।\nसंस्कृताः किल मन्त्रैश्च तेऽपि स्वर्गमवाप्नुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fires desire meat, so scripture is heard; animals are always killed at sacrifices, brahmin, by the twice-born, and, consecrated by mantras, they too reached heaven."}},{"n":10,"text":"यदि नैवाग्नयो ब्रह्मन्मांसकामाभवन्पुरा ।\nभक्ष्यं नैव भवेन्मांसं कस्यचिद्द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"If the fires had never wanted meat before, brahmin, meat would not be food for anyone, best of brahmins."}},{"n":11,"text":"अत्रापि विधिरुक्तश्च मुनिभिर्मांसभक्षणे ।\nदेवतानां पितॄणां च भुङ्क्ते दत्त्वा तु यः सदा ।\nयथाविधि यथाश्रद्धं न स दुष्यति भक्षणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here too the sages have laid down the rule for eating meat: one who always eats after giving to the gods and ancestors, by rule and with faith, is not stained by eating."}},{"n":12,"text":"अमांसाशी भवत्येवमित्यपि श्रूयते श्रुतिः ।\nभार्यां गच्छन्ब्रह्मचारी ऋतौ भवति ब्राह्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So scripture is heard that one becomes a non-meat-eater: a brahmin who approaches his wife in season is a celibate."}},{"n":13,"text":"सत्यानृते विनिश्चित्य अत्रापि विधिरुच्यते ।\nसौदासेन पुरा राज्ञा मानुषा भक्षिता द्विज ।\nशापाभिभूतेन भृशमत्र किं प्रतिभाति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having considered truth and falsehood, the rule is stated here too. Long ago King Saudasa, overcome by a curse, ate human beings, brahmin; what do you make of that?"}},{"n":14,"text":"स्वधर्म इति कृत्वा तु न त्यजामि द्विजोत्तम ।\nपुराकृतमिति ज्ञात्वा जीवाम्येतेन कर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Considering it my own dharma, I do not give it up, best of brahmins; knowing it as done in the past, I live by this work."}},{"n":15,"text":"स्वकर्म त्यजतो ब्रह्मन्नधर्म इह दृश्यते ।\nस्वकर्मनिरतो यस्तु स धर्म इति निश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one giving up his own work, brahmin, unrighteousness is seen here; one devoted to his own work, it is settled, has dharma."}},{"n":16,"text":"पूर्वं हि विहितं कर्म देहिनं न विमुञ्चति ।\nधात्रा विधिरयं दृष्टो बहुधा कर्मनिर्णये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Work ordained earlier does not release the embodied; this rule laid down by the creator is seen in many ways in deciding work."}},{"n":17,"text":"द्रष्टव्यं तु भवेत्प्राज्ञ क्रूरे कर्मणि वर्तता ।\nकथं कर्म शुभं कुर्यां कथं मुच्ये पराभवात् ।\nकर्मणस्तस्य घोरस्य बहुधा निर्णयो भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But it should be considered, wise one, by one engaged in cruel work: how can I do good work, how can I be freed from defeat? The decision about that terrible work can come in many ways."}},{"n":18,"text":"दाने च सत्यवाक्ये च गुरुशुश्रूषणे तथा ।\nद्विजातिपूजने चाहं धर्मे च निरतः सदा ।\nअतिवादातिमानाभ्यां निवृत्तोऽस्मि द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am always devoted to giving, truthful speech, serving the teacher, honouring brahmins and dharma; I have turned back from excess speech and from pride, best of brahmins."}},{"n":19,"text":"कृषिं साध्विति मन्यन्ते तत्र हिंसा परा स्मृता ।\nकर्षन्तो लाङ्गलैः पुंसो घ्नन्ति भूमिशयान्बहून् ।\nजीवानन्यांश्च बहुशस्तत्र किं प्रतिभाति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Farming is considered good, yet there the greatest violence is declared: men ploughing with ploughs kill many creatures that live in the earth, and many other beings; what do you think of that?"}},{"n":20,"text":"धान्यबीजानि यान्याहुर्व्रीह्यादीनि द्विजोत्तम ।\nसर्वाण्येतानि जीवानि तत्र किं प्रतिभाति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The seeds of grain they speak of, rice and others, best of brahmins, are all living beings; what do you think of that?"}},{"n":21,"text":"अध्याक्रम्य पशूंश्चापि घ्नन्ति वै भक्षयन्ति च ।\nवृक्षानथौषधीश्चैव छिन्दन्ति पुरुषा द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men also kill and eat animals after attacking them, and they cut trees and herbs, brahmin."}},{"n":22,"text":"जीवा हि बहवो ब्रह्मन्वृक्षेषु च फलेषु च ।\nउदके बहवश्चापि तत्र किं प्रतिभाति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many living things are in trees and fruits, brahmin, and many in the water; what do you think of that?"}},{"n":23,"text":"सर्वं व्याप्तमिदं ब्रह्मन्प्राणिभिः प्राणिजीवनैः ।\nमत्स्या ग्रसन्ते मत्स्यांश्च तत्र किं प्रतिभाति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this is pervaded by creatures that live on creatures, brahmin; fish swallow fish; what do you think of that?"}},{"n":24,"text":"सत्त्वैः सत्त्वानि जीवन्ति बहुधा द्विजसत्तम ।\nप्राणिनोऽन्योन्यभक्षाश्च तत्र किं प्रतिभाति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Beings live on beings in many ways, best of brahmins, and creatures eat one another; what do you think of that?"}},{"n":25,"text":"चङ्क्रम्यमाणा जीवांश्च धरणीसंश्रितान्बहून् ।\nपद्भ्यां घ्नन्ति नरा विप्र तत्र किं प्रतिभाति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Walking about, people kill with their feet many creatures that rest on the ground, brahmin; what do you think of that?"}},{"n":26,"text":"उपविष्टाः शयानाश्च घ्नन्ति जीवाननेकशः ।\nज्ञानविज्ञानवन्तश्च तत्र किं प्रतिभाति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sitting or lying down they kill creatures many times, even people of knowledge and learning; what do you think of that?"}},{"n":27,"text":"जीवैर्ग्रस्तमिदं सर्वमाकाशं पृथिवी तथा ।\nअविज्ञानाच्च हिंसन्ति तत्र किं प्रतिभाति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this sky and earth are filled with creatures, and people harm them without knowing; what do you think of that?"}},{"n":28,"text":"अहिंसेति यदुक्तं हि पुरुषैर्विस्मितैः पुरा ।\nके न हिंसन्ति जीवान्वै लोकेऽस्मिन्द्विजसत्तम ।\nबहु संचिन्त्य इह वै नास्ति कश्चिदहिंसकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When men long ago said with wonder \"non-violence\", who in this world does not harm living things, best of brahmins? Having thought much on it, here no one is non-violent."}},{"n":29,"text":"अहिंसायां तु निरता यतयो द्विजसत्तम ।\nकुर्वन्त्येव हि हिंसां ते यत्नादल्पतरा भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ascetics devoted to non-violence, best of brahmins, still commit violence; by effort it may become less."}},{"n":30,"text":"आलक्ष्याश्चैव पुरुषाः कुले जाता महागुणाः ।\nमहाघोराणि कर्माणि कृत्वा लज्जन्ति वै न च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men of noble family and great virtues are seen doing very terrible deeds without shame."}},{"n":31,"text":"सुहृदः सुहृदोऽन्यांश्च दुर्हृदश्चापि दुर्हृदः ।\nसम्यक्प्रवृत्तान्पुरुषान्न सम्यगनुपश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They do not see rightly the friends of their friends, others, or even enemies of their enemies, men who are acting rightly."}},{"n":32,"text":"समृद्धैश्च न नन्दन्ति बान्धवा बान्धवैरपि ।\nगुरूंश्चैव विनिन्दन्ति मूढाः पण्डितमानिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Relatives are not pleased with their prosperous relatives, and fools who think themselves learned even disparage their teachers."}},{"n":33,"text":"बहु लोके विपर्यस्तं दृश्यते द्विजसत्तम ।\nधर्मयुक्तमधर्मं च तत्र किं प्रतिभाति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Much that is reversed is seen in the world, best of brahmins, righteousness mixed with unrighteousness; what do you think of that?"}},{"n":34,"text":"वक्तुं बहुविधं शक्यं धर्माधर्मेषु कर्मसु ।\nस्वकर्मनिरतो यो हि स यशः प्राप्नुयान्महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Much can be said about the many kinds of dharma and adharma in actions; the one devoted to his own work gains great fame."}}]}]}